# --- secrets: NEVER commit ---
test-keys.env
*.env
!*.example.env

# --- nested git/bare repos ---
charon-rebuild-backup.git/

# --- ephemeral fleet runtime state (claims/submitted/done markers) ---
fleet/state/*
# ...except the persisted roadmap (canonical source for report.sh/handoff.sh).
!fleet/state/ROADMAP.tsv
# ...except the operator decision/action list (durable by design — a list that is
# lost on a fresh clone or a handoff is not a running list; operator decision 11,
# 2026-07-26). Read/written via fleet/pending.sh.
!fleet/state/OPERATOR-ACTIONS.md
# ...except the coverage-meta-gate rule registry (durable, git-tracked by design —
# consumed by fleet/checks/rule-coverage.sh; the §11 mechanized-coverage source of truth).
!fleet/state/RULE-REGISTRY.tsv
# ...except the REVIEWER-DOGFOOD-REDS ground-truth corpus (durable, git-tracked by
# design — see REDS-CORPUS.md's own OOB design note).
!fleet/state/REDS-CORPUS.md
# ...except the bidirectional rule-coverage audit register (RULE-SYNC-AUDIT
# ticket) — durable, derived from the sibling frameworks' inventories.
!fleet/state/RULE-SYNC-REGISTER.tsv
# ...except the config-drift source registry (CONFIG-SOURCES ticket) — local + gateway,
# durable; config-drift.sh reads this to detect provider siloing.
!fleet/state/CONFIG-SOURCES.tsv
# ...except the outcome-test blueprint + its adversarial review (operator-supplied proposal for
# test_gateway_outcome.py, 2026-08-02). Operator asked for this file to be DURABLE: it holds the
# verbatim proposal, the review that found it would pass on a gateway with no failover at all,
# and the corrected shape. A blueprint that lives only in a session transcript is not a blueprint.
!fleet/state/OUTCOME-TEST-BLUEPRINT.md
# ...except the service-liveness registry (SERVICE-LIVENESS-WATCHDOG) — the declarative SSOT of
# every supervised service. fleet/watchdog/ renders monit config + evaluates liveness FROM it;
# it is version-controlled config, NOT ephemeral runtime state, so it must survive the blanket ignore.
!fleet/state/service-registry.tsv
# ...except the registry META-CATALOG (REGISTRY-META-CATALOG ticket) — the durable INDEX of
# registries (index-only, not their data); reconciled by fleet/checks/discover-registries.sh.
!fleet/state/registry-catalog.tsv
# ...except the BENCH-PROVISIONAL-SCORING design of record (#20 — operator-led
# deep-dive 2026-07-16). Durable design artifact, sibling to PATH-C-DOGFOOD-EVAL
# / EVAL-TAXONOMY / EVAL-PIPELINE-DESIGN / S8-GRACEFUL-DEGRADE-DESIGN above;
# tracked so a build session / #26 rebase can read it without checking out a
# branch. (Other long-lived design docs in fleet/state/ are tracked; this
# exemption exists because the blanket `fleet/state/*` is otherwise more
# restrictive than the original design-doc pattern.)
!fleet/state/BENCH-PROVISIONAL-SCORING-DESIGN.md
# ...except the five durable artifacts owned by in-flight rig tickets. Landed AHEAD
# of those PRs deliberately: `.gitignore` is an anchor file, and four separate PRs
# (#97 #96 #93 #47) each appended their own negation here. Serialising them meant
# re-resolving the same conflict three times, and every merge invalidated the other
# branches' patch context. Landing all five negations up front dissolves the only
# contention edge in the open-PR set so the rest are file-disjoint.
!fleet/state/SSOT-REGISTRY.tsv
!fleet/state/REACHABILITY-AUDIT.md
!fleet/state/.reachability-allowlist
!fleet/state/provider-pricing-limits.tsv
!fleet/state/LAND-SH-POSTMORTEM.md
# ...and FREE-TIER-LIMITS.tsv (#116), which is currently tracked only because it was
# force-added; it had no negation line at all. Made explicit for consistency.
!fleet/state/FREE-TIER-LIMITS.tsv
# ...and the EVAL-REGISTRY tool-adoption source-of-record — a durable, append-only
# curated registry (sibling to REDS-CORPUS/RULE-SYNC-REGISTER above), referenced by the
# deep-dive eval docs and the tool-adoption sweep. Was living on-disk only (no negation);
# tracked now so the manager's land and every worktree carry it.
!fleet/state/EVAL-REGISTRY.md
# ...and the KSF linter-tools review — the durable eval that grounds the bandit/vulture
# adopt-vs-keep verdicts (product/stdlib scope vs rig CI scope). Was on-disk only; tracked
# now so the EVAL-REGISTRY bandit row's citation resolves in every checkout.
!fleet/state/KSF-LINTER-TOOLS-REVIEW.md
# ...and the shellcheck set-e tab-kill evaluation — the executed consult-first evidence behind
# the EVAL-REGISTRY shellcheck row (LAUNCHER-GATE-SETE-KILL). Tracked so that row's
# evidence-link resolves in every checkout rather than only on the authoring box.
!fleet/state/SHELLCHECK-SETE-EVAL.md
# ...and the work-loop-integrity research (deep-research evidence base for WORKLOOP-INTEGRITY-STACK-SPIKE).
!fleet/state/WORKLOOP-INTEGRITY-RESEARCH.md
# ...and the canonical numeric priority axis (PRIORITY-CONSOLIDATION ticket) — the band table
# + selection-ladder reference that claim.sh, validate_board.sh, and the drift test all key
# off. Sibling to RULE-REGISTRY / ROADMAP / REDS-CORPUS as a git-tracked, single-source-of-truth
# design artifact. Tracked so every worktree sees the same axis (the whole point of consolidation
# is to kill the 3-way drift that existed when the doc was on-disk only).
!fleet/state/PRIORITY-LADDER.md
# ...and the Faktory adoption record (FAKTORY-ADOPT ticket) — durable adopt record + real
# durability-proof evidence for the sole job/lease substrate. The blanket fleet/state/* ignore
# would otherwise silently drop it; same anchor pattern as the tracked state docs above.
!fleet/state/FAKTORY-ADOPT.md
# ...and the tier-drift HARD-FAIL set (TIER-BALANCE ticket) — the config that gives the
# validate_board 2f tier-drift gate its teeth. Without this file every mismatch is an
# advisory WARN and the gate cannot go RED in any configuration, which is exactly the
# defect it shipped with. It MUST be tracked or the gate silently reverts to advisory.
!fleet/state/tier-drift-red.txt
# ...and the preflight ownership ruling (PREFLIGHT-OWNS-ARBITRATE) — the arbitration that
# cleared the board's 5-way fleet/preflight.sh owns-collision. Durable decision record.
!fleet/state/PREFLIGHT-OWNERSHIP-RULING.md

# --- KSF tool local runtime store (SQLite DB regenerated by the tool; NOT source) ---
.ksf/

# --- scratch / logs ---
*.log
fleet/logs/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
fleet/state/overnight/

# auto-gen REDS registry (regenerated by build-rig; never source-tracked)
fleet/reds.tsv

# runtime artifacts (regenerated; never source-tracked)
fleet/scorecard.v1.json
fleet/provider-exhaustion-ledger.tsv
fleet/model-scorecard.tsv
# ...and the reachability audit (REACHABILITY-GATE analysis; referenced by handoffs).
!fleet/state/REACHABILITY-AUDIT.md
# ...and the SG-ISSUE-CONTROL-PLANE design of record (SG-ISSUE-CONTROL-PLANE ticket `owns:` this
# path). Tracked deliberately, not force-added: with no negation the file was INVISIBLE to
# `git status`, which is exactly how a 639-line revision silently REPLACED the 109-line design
# of record without a reviewable diff (PR #257 review F1). A design git cannot see is not a
# design of record. See the doc's §7 for the location decision and the alternatives rejected.
!fleet/state/DESIGN-SG-ISSUE-CONTROL-PLANE.md

# regenerable code map (rebuilt by the wired graphify-freshness gate) — do not track (matches product)
graphify-out/
!fleet/state/lens-registry.tsv
# ...and the 2026-08-01 tool-utilization audit — the ~20%%-of-installed-capability measurement
!fleet/state/TOOL-UTILIZATION-AUDIT.md
# ...and the cross-session carry-forward TODO — the list the next session must read FIRST.
!fleet/state/PRIORITY-TODO.md
# ...and the rescued CATALOG-REFRESH-PERSIST WIP patch (droid killed at 2026-08-01 session close).
!fleet/state/RESCUE-catalog-refresh-persist-WIP.patch
!fleet/state/GATE-DEFECT-OWNERSHIP-DIAG.md
# ...and the previous-session retrospective — the durable record of what the last session did
# wrong and the command/rule that fixes each. Blanket fleet/state/* would keep it on-disk only,
# which is the exact failure mode it documents (§F11: state that dies with the session).
!fleet/state/SESSION-RETRO-PREV.md

# Stray git worktrees must never be COMMITTED. A worktree dir that gets `git add`ed is recorded
# as a GITLINK (mode 160000) with no .gitmodules entry, which makes every CI checkout fail with
# "fatal: No url found for submodule path ... in .gitmodules" -> git exit 128 -> rig-ci RED on
# every PR. Happened 2026-08-02 with .worktrees/preflight-daemon-seam and silently broke the
# merge gate. This is the worktree-leak class landing in the repo itself.
.worktrees/

# ...and rescued WIP backups. A "backup" inside the blanket fleet/state/* ignore is NOT durable —
# that mistake was made twice on 2026-08-02. Negated so a rescue survives a fresh clone.
!fleet/state/wip-backup-*/
!fleet/state/wip-backup-*/**

# ...and session handoffs — the file the next session reads FIRST. A handoff inside the blanket
# fleet/state/* ignore is a handoff that does not survive a fresh clone.
!fleet/state/HANDOFF-*.md
# ...and multi-session PLANs (same reasoning as handoffs, and the same failure this rig keeps
# hitting: "a decision that lives only in a session's memory is not a decision"). A plan that is
# held across sessions for an operator decision must survive a fresh clone.
!fleet/state/PLAN-*.md
# ...and THE OPERATOR DECISION LEDGER — the single most important durable file in the repo. Six
# other mechanisms failed to make decisions stick (see the file's own table); a decision ledger
# that does not survive a fresh clone would be the seventh.
!fleet/state/DECISIONS.md
# ...and the Lane C three-axis tool re-evaluation (D-009). 120 lines of measured re-scoring that
# would otherwise live only in a session transcript — the exact failure D-007 names.
!fleet/state/LANE-C-*.md
